                <pb facs="0582" n="1236" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1236"/>

                <head>No. 576.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing to Mr. Fish</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 4, 1874</date>.
                        (Received December 4.)</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Secretary of State, Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Long note received from Ulloa at twelve last night, which discusses the legal
                    questions from his point of view, but concedes indemnity to the United States on
                    the same basis as to Great Britain, and also trial of local authorities
                    implicated. Telegram of details in preparation.</p>
                <closer><signed>CUSHING.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
